4. Student Table

Field	Data Type	Key	Description
StudentID	INT	PK	Unique student identifier
Name	VARCHAR(100)		Student’s name
Email	VARCHAR(150)		Student’s email address

Primary Key

StudentID

The StudentID uniquely identifies each student.

⸻

5. Task Table

Field	Data Type	Key	Description
TaskID	INT	PK	Unique task identifier
StudentID	INT	FK	Student who owns the task
Title	VARCHAR(200)		Task title
Description	TEXT		Task details
DueDate	DATE		Task deadline
IsCompleted	BOOLEAN		Completion status

Primary Key

TaskID

The TaskID uniquely identifies each task.

Foreign Key

StudentID references Student(StudentID).

⸻

6. Relationships

A student can have many tasks.

Therefore:

Student 1 ─────────── * Task

This is a one-to-many relationship.

One student can create multiple tasks, while each task belongs to one student.

⸻

7. Example SQL

The following SQL demonstrates the proposed database structure:

CREATE TABLE Student (
    StudentID INT PRIMARY KEY,
    Name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    Email VARCHAR(150) NOT NULL
);
CREATE TABLE Task (
    TaskID INT PRIMARY KEY,
    StudentID INT NOT NULL,
    Title VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,
    Description TEXT,
    DueDate DATE,
    IsCompleted BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
    FOREIGN KEY (StudentID)
        REFERENCES Student(StudentID)
);

