9. Database Normalization

The proposed design separates student information from task information.

This prevents repeating the student’s name and email for every task and makes the database easier to maintain.

⸻

10. Future Database Implementation

The database can be implemented in a future version using:

* SQLite
* SQL Server
* MySQL

The C# application can then use a database connection to save and retrieve tasks permanently.

⸻

11. Conclusion

The proposed database design supports the main requirements of the Student Task Manager. It provides a simple structure for storing students and their tasks while allowing the system to be expanded in future versions.
